.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_STREAM_EXCHANGE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_stream_exchange
.Nd route a stream's records between workers
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fo dtfl_stream_exchange
.Fa "dtfl_stream *st"
.Fa "uint64_t (*route)(const void *rec, size_t len, void *ctx)"
.Fa "void *ctx"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_stream_exchange
produces a stream whose records are the records of
.Fa st
redistributed across the workers.
Each record is sent to the worker that
.Fa route
returns for it, modulo the number of peers.
When
.Fa route
is
.Dv NULL ,
the record type's hash is used.
Records are forwarded unchanged, at their original time, so the output
stream carries the input's record type.
.Pp
.Fa ctx
is passed to
.Fa route
on every call; it is not owned by the operator.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_stream_exchange
returns the exchanged stream, owned by the scope.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static uint64_t by_key(const void *rec, size_t len, void *ctx) {
	return dtfl_get_u64(rec);
}

dtfl_stream *shuffled = dtfl_stream_exchange(in, by_key, NULL);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn dtfl_stream_exchange
does not return an error code.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_stream_concat 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_count 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_map 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_partition 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_to_stream 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
This is the C form of timely's
.Fn exchange
operator.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
The operator and its stream belong to the worker thread that built them.
The record movement across workers happens inside the worker's steps,
through the communication layer, not through this call.
